Explanation:

1. In single‐input mode, `this.inputField` (and thus `inputFrom`) can end up being `null`.  
2. The Flatpickr “fixEvents” plugin was unconditionally calling `inputFrom.addEventListener(...)`, causing a crash when `inputFrom` is missing.  
3. By guarding both `release()` and `init()` with `if (inputFrom && inputFrom.addEventListener/removeEventListener) { … }`, the plugin no longer blows up when only one input is present.
